Patch 02: mount MarginObjectLayer on tenant sites, desktop-only (src/app/sites/_shared/site-client.tsx)

Rationale: today MarginObjectLayer is mounted only on the PING
homepage (src/app/page.tsx). Tenant sites get no object intelligence.
This patch mounts the same layer on tenant site pages with
descriptors built from the already-serialized PUBLIC graph (the
publicGraph() boundary in src/app/sites/happy-place/page.tsx is
untouched; private objects never enter client state).

Binding compliance:
- The wrapper renders the layer only at viewport width >= 1024px.
  Tablet (768-1023) keeps the layer's own compact edge-rail policy.
  Below 768 the layer is not mounted at all: mobile gets object
  depth through inline cards + ObjectOverlay (patch 03), never
  floating chrome, never a drawer in primary UX.
- Anchor map (anchorKey = section id, requires patch 01):
  Services sections -> service objects; People -> person objects;
  Locations -> location objects; ObjectFeed/Posts -> post/article
  objects; BusinessSummary -> owner object; Hero and Contact ->
  no rail.
- Descriptor fields (name, category, location, whyHere) are read
  from evidence-backed public graph fields only; nulls omit the
  line, never guessed (MarginObjectDescriptor contract in
  src/fyd/ui/object-layer/types.ts).

